Apache HTTP Server Installation
1. System Preparation

    sudo dnf update - Update system packages
    
    sudo dnf install httpd - Install Apache web server

2. Service Management

    sudo systemctl start httpd - Start Apache service
    
    sudo systemctl enable httpd - Enable auto-start on boot
    
    sudo systemctl restart httpd - Restart after configuration changes

3. Firewall Configuration

    sudo firewall-cmd --add-service=http --permanent - Allow HTTP traffic
    
    sudo firewall-cmd --reload - Apply firewall changes

4. Verification

    Access http://your_server_ip in web browser - Check default test page

5. Directory Structure

    /etc/httpd/ - Main configuration directory
    
    /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf - Primary configuration file
    
    /etc/httpd/conf.d/ - Additional configuration files
    
    /var/www/html/ - Default web content directory

Virtual Host Configuration
1. Create Site Directories

    sudo mkdir -p /var/www/html/example1 - Create directory for site 1
    
    sudo mkdir -p /var/www/html/example2 - Create directory for site 2

2. Set Permissions

    sudo chown -R apache:apache /var/www/html/example1 - Set Apache ownership
    
    sudo chown -R apache:apache /var/www/html/example2 - Set Apache ownership

3. Create Virtual Host Files

    sudo nano /etc/httpd/conf.d/example1.conf - Create config for first site
    
    sudo nano /etc/httpd/conf.d/example2.conf - Create config for second site

4. Virtual Host Configuration Example

    apache
    <VirtualHost *:80>
      ServerAdmin webmaster@example1.com
      DocumentRoot /var/www/html/example1
      ServerName example1.com
      ServerAlias www.example1.com
      ErrorLog /var/log/httpd/example1-error.log
      CustomLog /var/log/httpd/example1-access.log combined
    </VirtualHost>
5. Validation & Activation

    sudo apachectl configtest - Check configuration syntax
    
    sudo systemctl restart httpd - Apply configuration changes

6. DNS Setup

Configure domain DNS records to point to server IP address

SSL/TLS Certificate Setup
1. Installation

    sudo dnf install httpd mod_ssl certbot python3-certbot-apache - Install required packages

2. Verify SSL Module

    sudo apachectl -M | grep ssl - Check if mod_ssl is enabled

    sudo a2enmod ssl - Enable SSL module (if not active)

3. Obtain Certificates

    sudo certbot --apache -d example.com -d www.example.com - Get certificates for domain

4. Certificate Renewal

    sudo certbot renew --dry-run - Test automatic renewal process

    Auto-renewal: Certbot configures automatic renewal by default

5. Firewall for HTTPS

    sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=https - Allow HTTPS traffic

    sudo firewall-cmd --reload - Apply firewall changes

6. SSL Verification

    openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 - Test SSL connection
    
    Access https://example.com in browser - Verify HTTPS works

7. Security Hardening (Optional)

    Enable HSTS (HTTP Strict Transport Security)
    
    Implement security headers

Regular system and software updates
